{"body":"Legacy identity: `FOS-000002`. Original source: [immutable historical definition](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/73f891d6c0cf498ac92e804d7d0f0cd344a083f5/local-docs/reviews/observability-sweep.md).\n\nShared requirements and grouping: https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/issues/8. All original criteria below remain required. Source status statements below describe their historical revision; current delivery evidence is recorded separately. Original relative links are resolved below.\n\n## Original definition (verbatim)\n\n2. **FOS-000002 — Make utility parse failure affect the command result.** **S per tool; no dependencies; §2–§3.** Start with [list:266](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/556da9ff7d7616704dda515756219ab1dab693ec/cli/fossilize_list.cpp#L266), then [rehash:226](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/556da9ff7d7616704dda515756219ab1dab693ec/cli/fossilize_rehash.cpp#L226) and [prune:1003](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/556da9ff7d7616704dda515756219ab1dab693ec/cli/fossilize_prune.cpp#L1003), one small change each. Each logs a failed parse and proceeds toward success (E8). Retain partial output if useful, but return nonzero and identify incomplete scope; never print an ordinary empty connectivity row as a verified empty dependency set. **Check:** version rejection and invalid JSON; valid empty databases still succeed. Later apply the same rule to opt/disasm. Keep fallback optimization policy explicit rather than making an error-level message alone decide failure.\n\n   **Required automated success criteria — pending implementation:**\n\n   - **CLI subprocess regression tests, per migrated tool:** E8 version rejection and invalid JSON return nonzero and identify incomplete scope; valid populated and valid empty inputs return zero. List connectivity does not emit a rejected item as an ordinary verified empty dependency row.\n   - **Partial-output and policy tests:** A valid item followed by an invalid item preserves any promised partial output but never returns success. An explicitly permitted optimizer fallback returns the declared outcome and remains distinguishable from an unhandled parse failure when that tool is migrated.\n\n<!-- fossilize-migration-v1:FOS-000002 -->\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOVZpjbc8AAAABgs9uig","author":{"login":"robinwassen"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Readiness for review; issue remains open pending implementation PR and merge.\n\nIndependent work-unit checker accepted candidate feaa495218d16fa3dbe3e1b6f814f1abcf0bf9dd: all73 CTests passed in each Linux Debug/Release x exceptions OFF/ON configuration; six original-defect failures and six populated/empty baseline controls verified; all130 harness methods and103 explicit scenarios passed, with exact union and skill validation. Native Windows remains unverified; opt/disasm and optimizer fallback migration remain conditional future scope.\n\nCandidate: `feaa495218d16fa3dbe3e1b6f814f1abcf0bf9dd`; base: `36b78637e847463c4f58758a907b33ce5bf07ce5`; plan: `1`; issue input: `7c1ac13dac979fdfaa8f8945308a25c5bc161a999a81d6aad3b31e13fce847b7`.\n\nProposed source compare (branch will be published after final checking): https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/compare/master...codex/issue-11-utility-parse-results\n\n<!-- harness-ready:issue-11-20261029-parse-results:411d626c0c5f145d8fc0367cded186a8cccb5572ce06c691b3a13833e52001df -->\n\n<!-- harness-operation:050532181d9ed075dc4e62388294ee79d6db5c8c4620f41ddb92b576cafc3042 -->\n","createdAt":"2026-10-29T06:25:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/issues/11#issuecomment-6489599626","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":11,"state":"OPEN","title":"FOS-000002 — Make utility parse failure affect the command result","url":"https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/issues/11"}

